1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,132
There are places that cannot be
reduced to lines on a map...

2
00:00:06,212 --> 00:00:09,712
places that live in us before we
ever live in them.

3
00:00:09,792 --> 00:00:12,520
And Palestine... is one of those places.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,636
Here, the land was never just
a place to live...

5
00:00:17,716 --> 00:00:23,520
it was a home, a memory, a name passed down
from one generation to the next.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,463
In the villages, bread comes out of the taboun with the
first light, as it has for generations...

7
00:00:30,543 --> 00:00:34,520
and the seasons gather families around the
fields and threshing floors.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,260
In the cities, Jaffa's oranges
crossed the sea,

9
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:44,520
and Jerusalem, Haifa, Nablus and Gaza were
alive with markets and schools.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,542
It was an ordinary life... like that of
any people on their own land.

11
00:00:51,622 --> 00:00:52,520
Until 1948.

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,258
Amid the war of that year, as the British Mandate
ended and the State of Israel was established,

13
00:00:59,338 --> 00:01:03,369
more than seven hundred thousand Palestinians were
displaced from their towns and villages,

14
00:01:03,449 --> 00:01:05,809
and hundreds of villages were
emptied of their people.

15
00:01:05,889 --> 00:01:08,520
Palestinians call what happened the
Nakba — the Catastrophe.

16
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,324
They carried what they could...

17
00:01:12,404 --> 00:01:17,520
and many believed their absence would
last no more than a few days.

18
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,536
That is why many of them kept the
keys to their homes.

19
00:01:23,616 --> 00:01:27,554
An old iron key... that no
longer opens a door,

20
00:01:27,634 --> 00:01:29,520
but still opens memory.

21
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,688
Old photographs, names of villages
told to grandchildren...

22
00:01:34,768 --> 00:01:38,520
Here, memory is not only longing. It
is a trust handed down.

23
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,314
Today, a new generation carries that
trust in their school bags...

24
00:01:45,394 --> 00:01:47,520
alongside books and dreams.

25
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,037
Every autumn, families return to
the olive groves...

26
00:01:53,117 --> 00:01:56,520
as if renewing an old
promise with the land.

27
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,667
In the cities, life moves to
its daily rhythm:

28
00:02:00,747 --> 00:02:03,176
markets and cafés, students and workers...

29
00:02:03,256 --> 00:02:06,520
life that goes on, despite
checkpoints and restrictions.

30
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,874
On the shore of the
Mediterranean stands Gaza...

31
00:02:11,954 --> 00:02:14,028
narrow in land, vast in its people.

32
00:02:14,108 --> 00:02:18,520
Its fishermen head out to sea before dawn,
in search of the day's living.

33
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,862
Gaza has known siege, wars
and displacement...

34
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:26,124
yet every morning, life there
tries to begin again:

35
00:02:26,204 --> 00:02:32,520
a mother braiding her daughter's hair, a young man
carrying his books, a vendor arranging his goods.

36
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:38,810
Behind the news and the numbers,
there is a human being...

37
00:02:38,890 --> 00:02:42,520
with a name, a home,
memories... and dreams.

38
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,145
That is the story... like an
ancient olive tree:

39
00:02:47,225 --> 00:02:49,228
its roots run deep in the land,

40
00:02:49,308 --> 00:02:52,520
and whenever a branch is cut,
it grows a new one.

41
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,890
Palestine is not a line on a map...

42
00:02:55,970 --> 00:03:01,520
it is the story of a people, the memory of a home, and a
human being who has never stopped dreaming.

43
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:07,690
And this story has one name:

44
00:03:07,770 --> 00:03:09,520
Palestine.
